## Detailed Evidence

### Step 1: Utility Dedup — [shared/scalars.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/shared/scalars.ts)

**Canonical shared module created** at [shared/scalars.ts](file:///\\wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/shared/scalars.ts) exporting: `nowSec`, `toFiniteNumber`, `toFiniteNumberOr`, `clampInt`, `clampIntOr`.

**Also created:** [shared/challenges/mailbox.ts](file:///\\wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/shared/challenges/mailbox.ts) exporting `normalizeChallengeMailboxCategory`.

**Import adoption:** 34 imports use `shared/` paths; only 2 non-shared imports remain.

> [!WARNING]
> **5 local function copies still exist** (not just imports — actual `function` definitions):
> - `clampInt` in `globalSettingsAdmin.ts`, `adminActivity.ts`, `griftRetention.ts`, `adminScout/support.ts`
> - `toFiniteNumber` in `clickhouseSync.ts`, `adminScout/support.ts`, `allocationEngine.ts`
> - `normalizeChallengeMailboxCategory` in `challengeEvaluationSupport.ts`, `traderTalent.ts`

Per [.agents/audit-decomposition.md](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/.agents/audit-decomposition.md) rule: *"local wrappers are allowed when semantics differ"* — some of these have different signatures (e.g., `allocationEngine.toFiniteNumber` returns `number | null` vs the shared version). Each would need a case-by-case review.

